      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Of course! Alveolar fricatives are a category of speech sounds. In the case of the /s/ sound, the vocal cords do not vibrate, making it unvoiced. For the /z/ sound, the vocal cords vibrate during pronunciation, which makes it voiced. In essence, the difference lies in the vibration of the vocal cords: one unvoiced, one voiced.",
